Center News, to keep up to date with

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.080
what's happening in the industry. Link

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.640
in the description below. One way to

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.600
talk about capabilities is looking at

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.360
the famous blog by Tim Urban, Wait But

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.080
Why. And in his blog post, which is

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.400
already 11 years old, he introduced a

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.000
framework of ANI to AGI to ASI. ANI

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.280
refers to narrow intelligence, where AI

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.840
specializes on one narrow area. But

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.360
making the leap from ANI to AGI is a

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.440
much different and much more typical

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.640
case because general intelligence is

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.720
less about a collection of narrow

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.960
intelligence into one domain. Tim wrote

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.200
about how building an AGI is hard since

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.280
it's a computer that's as smart as

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.720
humans in general, not just one narrow

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.040
specialty. So, AGI is a completely

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.240
different problem than ANI. That's why

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.280
when we talk about AGI only in the

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.440
capabilities axis, measuring whether we

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.840
reach AGI by listing some arbitrary

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.560
tasks that AGI can't do is a weak

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.680
argument. In other words, we could have

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.440
reached AGI while still underperforming

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.360
some narrow domain tasks that ANI could

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.360
do better because general intelligence

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.600
is more about its ability to transfer

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.120
its learning and adapt to new situations

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.520
than having any task that it can do best

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.440
at. So, rather than listing arbitrary

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.120
tasks like fixing bathrooms,

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.520
babysitting, or doing the laundry, the

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.120
capabilities we should really be

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.560
measuring is how well it can transfer

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.800
knowledge, how well it can reason, and

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.640
how well it actually adapts to changing

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.440
environments. Now, after seeing this

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.080
progression, you might have concluded

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.240
that this entire debate around whether

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.640
we reached AGI or not is kind of

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.280
pointless. And you're not alone in this

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.960
since many people agree on that

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.960
sentiment. Dario from Anthropic thinks

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.120
that AGI is just a marketing term.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.919
Though, ironically, he goes ahead and

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:20.080
uses more marketing terms like saying

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.960
that we will soon have a country of

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.240
geniuses in a data center, whatever that

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.360
means. But whether or not the term AGI

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.440
is important in a scientific sense or

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:31.000
not, we can't really deny that it has a

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.160
huge economical weight to the term given

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.040
how so many tech CEOs are promising AGI

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.440
as something that we'll achieve in the

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.600
next 5 to 10 years. And this isn't the

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.640
first time people in the AI industry

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.880
were over-promised. Looking back at two

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.480
AI winters that can both be

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.880
characterized by hopes and promises that

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.400
ended up under-delivering. While

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.440
generative AI is certainly different

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.600
compared to previous iterations, given

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:57.440
just how powerful it already is, AGI is

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.560
not just a scientific hypothesis now,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.160
but it has a huge economical narrative

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.200
built into it, which makes it really

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.720
difficult to not talk about AGI, given

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.960
that our goal towards AGI currently

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.320
shapes how we allocate funding, how we

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.360
value AI companies, the infrastructure

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.440
spending into data centers, and hiring

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.480
top talents and engineers. So, because

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.320
all these companies have different ways

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:21.919
to measure AGI, by definition, different

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:23.919
companies should then reach AGI at

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:25.640
different moments. Just like how Jensen

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.800
recently said that OpenAI did achieve

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.400
AGI with Astra using Nvidia chips.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.680
Emphasis on the using Nvidia chips. But,

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.560
what matters less is a definition of

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.080
what AGI is, but more that we continue

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.159
our progress forward and manage our

00:08:39.159 --> 00:08:41.479
expectation in the meantime on what AGI

00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:43.360
could really mean. And kicking the can

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.320
down the road and moving the goalpost

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.120
only risks repeating the same cycle all

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.960
over again. And I'm sure that people

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.680
will get tired of hearing the same

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.480
narrative over and over again that says

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:55.760
the future is only 5 years from today. I

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.360
think it's important to keep in mind

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.839
that the first AGI model might be less

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:01.880
capable than other models that we

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.120
already have that's closer to ANI. This

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.880
definitely raises some concern to me

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.280
about managing people's expectation

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.400
since AGI is building up to this very

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.240
thing that certainly will change

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:13.920
everything overnight, which I don't

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.080
believe would be the case.